      <activity id="692e5573-36e6-503b-8429-7b2879cdcf60" activityNameId="d67b59a2-ea79-54e2-9567-e4eeb415917e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, at cogen 1MWth, diesel, allocation exergy</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, at cogen 1MWth, diesel, allocation exergy
Inventory for 1 MJ heat from diesel, burned in a cogeneration unit with a capacity of 1 MWth. The multioutput process "diesel, burned in cogen 1MWth delivers the coproducts "heat, at cogen 1MWth, diesel, allocation exergy" and "electricity, at cogen 1MWth, diesel, allocation exergy". The energy efficiency is 44% for electricity and 42% for heat. The exergy factor is 1 for ectricity and 0.170 for heat. This leads to the allocation factor of 0.86 for electricity an 0.14 for heat.;
UUID: 81a546af-86a9-3f87-8e76-9b98fe1bbf42
Included are the diesel burning in a 1 MWth cogen unit which in turn includes fuel input, infrastructure (boiler), air and water emissions and electrictiy needed for operation. The efficiency and allocation according to exergy is considered
Location: Data apply to the combustion in Switzerland.
Technology: efficiency of average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_81a546af-86a9-3f87-8e76-9b98fe1bbf42.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
